{
  "id": "rev-007",
  "description": "(0.5.0) Known-answer vectors for the RFC-ACDP-0014 §7 key_revocation classification (stable rule anchors acdp.rule.revocation-classification, acdp.rule.revocation-fold, acdp.rule.revocation-scope and acdp.rule.revocation-precedence in registries/rule-anchors.md). Each vector gives already-verified inputs for one context signed by key fingerprint F at one vantage, and the expected stage result. The inputs are: the context's agent_id and F; its registry receipt (null = none; verified flag, RFC-ACDP-0010 §8 receipt-key status, receipt-attested created_at); the revocation lineage members found, each already signature-verified per §5; and how many other lookups were unknown (§8). scripts/conformance-runner.py executes the classification and compares it with expected. Signature, DID and receipt verification are out of scope here (rev-001, rcpt-*, rot-*).",
  "tags": [
    "revocation",
    "consumer",
    "0.5.0",
    "known-answer"
  ],
  "applies_to_profiles": [
    "acdp-consumer"
  ],
  "input": {
    "rules": "Applicable = members whose type is key-revocation or acdp:key-revocation (§10 equivalence), whose revoked_key_fingerprint is F, and that are in producer scope (producer-signed: agent_id equals the context's agent_id; registry-attested: revoked_key_controller equals it). Retracted members count. Other members are ignored and never disarm. T = the earliest compromised_since among applicable members; the attributed revocation is the one carrying it (vectors have no ties). No applicable member gives not-revoked. Otherwise: no receipt, a failed receipt, or a historical receipt key gives unplaceable; receipt created_at < T gives pre-compromise; else revoked. Combine with unknown lookups by refusal (revoked, unplaceable) > unknown > pre-compromise > not-revoked."
  },
  "scenarios": [
    {
      "name": "A — classify every vector",
      "expected": {
        "behavior": "For each vector, the implementation's key_revocation stage reports the expected class, the effective boundary T and the attributed revocation ctx_id (boundary and ctx_id are null for not-revoked and unknown)."
      }
    }
  ],
  "vectors": [
